        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue! I [struggled to find a real world LSP server](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2372#issuecomment-4269304031) that uses `command`. Glad to know that `vtsls` does.\n\n> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) I debugged it, on the non-snippet path, `item` doesn't have client_id so it fail on `vim.lsp.get_client_by_id`\n\nThat was indeed the case, thanks. However, this showed a bit bigger problem in that `completionItem/resolve` request parameters included `client_id` field which was added by 'mini.completion' and does not comply to LSP spec. Handling it slightly cleaner seems to have resolved this issue on latest `main`.",
